    "result_text": "The implementation is complete and verified. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner response. It returns `true` when **any** of the three conditions hold, else `false`:\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2014 the persisted `possibleDuplicate` flag is set (set by `FlagPossibleDuplicate` when the owner shares an existing owner's phonetic surname + postcode with a different identity).\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email** \u2014 the email domain's second-level label matches a known throw-away mail keyword (e.g. `mailinator.net`, `tempmail.io`, `throwaway-*`). The hard blocklist (`mailinator.com`, etc.) is already rejected at create with 400, so this deliberately catches the *adjacent* cases that survive to persistence.\n3. **City over soft capacity** \u2014 the persisted `capacityWarning` flag is set. Since a city at/over the hard cap of 50 is rejected before persistence, a persisted `capacityWarning` (40\u201349) is exactly \"over the soft capacity of 40.\"\n\n### Changes\n- **`mapper/RiskFlag.java`** (new) \u2014 pure helper `RiskFlag.of(Owner)` computing the flag from persisted owner state, so it recomputes identically on `GET` read-back. Follows the existing standalone-helper convention (`OwnerSegment`, `CityRegion`, `MemberId`).\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression wiring `riskFlag` to `RiskFlag.of(owner)`.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (generates the DTO field), with a description spelling out all three heuristics.\n\n### Verification\n- `./mvnw -o compile` \u2014 clean.\n- Confirmed generated `OwnerDto` has `riskFlag` and `OwnerMapperImpl` calls `RiskFlag.of(owner)`.\n- `./mvnw -o test` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (`AcceptanceTest.coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` \u2014 a normal `@example.test` owner returns `riskFlag: false`).\n\nNote: the one existing test only pins the `false` case; the two ambiguous terms in the spec (\"disposable-adjacent\", \"soft capacity\") aren't pinned by tests or prior code, so I chose principled definitions anchored to the existing blocklist and capacity thresholds and documented them fully in the OpenAPI field description.",
